   "skos:definition": "Israeli-American psychologist (1934-2024) who co-founded the heuristics-and-biases program with Amos Tversky, won the 2002 Nobel Prize in economics, and popularized the fast/slow (System 1 / System 2) account of intuition and deliberation.",
